            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a co-parent-in-law, then the Tamil for a mother’s younger sister."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பங்காளி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பங்காளி — paṅkāḷi — \"a paternal kinsman; a partner\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "திருவிழாவுக்கு எல்லாப் பங்காளிகளும் வந்தார்கள். tiruviḻāvukku ellāp paṅkāḷikaḷum vantārkaḷ. All our kinsmen came to the festival."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: பங்காளிகள், paṅkāḷikaḷ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பங்கு \"a share\" + -ஆளி \"one who\": those who share an inheritance. Also a business partner."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பங்காளி (paṅkāḷi) is a native compound of பங்கு paṅku, \"a share\" (DEDR 3808), and -ஆளி, \"one who has\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
